      "native_actual_text_bytes_exact": true,
      "independent_derivation": "For q^2=i*omega*mu*zeta and (Laplacian-q^2)G=-delta, E=(Hessian-q^2 I)G*m/zeta yields the -i*omega*mu*m delta source and curl E=-i*omega*mu*(grad G cross m). This expands to the stated dyadic coefficients; no sigma-only E branch is called. Partition AII eI+AIB gB=bI gives new correction -AIB*gB. The complex receiver is ordinary linear, not conjugate linear.",
