      "static_findings": [
        "Explicit E uses full admittivity and the reviewed dyadic coefficients; positive real-space separation checked before division and targets blocked128/source count<=512.",
        "New nonaxis curl-E/H control uses the selected two five-point finite differences and unchanged1e-5 screen. New whole incidence-row closure tests the frozen receiver trace against nodal gradients.",
        "New E line integral and receiver-edge reference use frozen S1 moments and H voltages; no old primary/H integration or C/A construction. Receiver interpolation error is reported rather than cancelled or tuned away.",
        "Boundary stage evaluates only new Born E for selected tangential edges and fixed source/edge pairs. Actual stage exactly partitions saved A/AII and constructs only -AIB*gB, then one COLAMD solve.",
        "Corrected voltage uses ordinary complex-linear trace. Existing S1 zero-boundary field remains immutable; no old forcing or wire residual is added.",
        "Stage cache and temp paths remain stage-local, output is exclusive, all stage source pins read back, previous success and free-memory preconditions precede the next stage."
      ],
